# 4. ABSOLUTE RULE — USER CATEGORY PRIORITY

This is the highest-priority classification requirement.

**If the owner manually selects a category or subcategory, automatic classification must never override it.**

Classification precedence, from highest to lowest:

| Priority | Classification source |
|---|---|
| 1 | Explicit owner-selected category during Add/Import |
| 2 | Previously saved manual category assignment with active manual lock |
| 3 | Owner-approved source-folder-to-category mapping |
| 4 | Owner-defined exact URL or more-specific path/domain rules |
| 5 | Initial source-folder seed mappings |
| 6 | Generic domain, URL path, title, description and keyword rules |
| 7 | Uncategorized / Needs Manual Review |

